<h2>A cardamom-anchored Gulf market</h2>
<p>Kuwait stands out in our data specifically for cardamom — a smaller population market than Saudi Arabia or the UAE, but a genuinely significant destination for Indian cardamom by value. Mango, garlic and fresh onion round out the picture in smaller volumes.</p>

<h2>Short transit, straightforward terms</h2>
<p>Shuwaikh and Shuaiba are both reachable in roughly 4-7 days from Indian west-coast ports, keeping this a practical route for both staple commodities and shorter-shelf-life produce. The Kuwaiti Dinar has historically been one of the more stable Gulf currencies, and USD-denominated pricing is standard practice on this lane.</p>

